            "review_text": "Mai T\n8 contributions\n0\nHidden Omakase Treasure at an Unbeatable Price\nJan 2024 • Family\nWhenever I feel worn out after a long day at work and need a pick-me-up that doesn't empty my wallet, this is my go-to place. Tucked away in the small alley of Thai Van Lung, this sushi spot is a real find. It's a no-frills, upstairs space that delivers a genuine omakase experience without breaking the bank.\n\nThe sushi selection impresses with its variety, showcasing an array of fish types and intricate preparation methods. The chef's dedication and expertise are evident in each meticulously crafted piece. Starting at just 900K VND, the omakase menu is surprisingly budget-friendly, especially considering the quality and range offered. For those looking to indulge a bit more, the 1.5 mil VND option adds luxurious treats like wagyu to the mix, making it an excellent value for such a lavish and comprehensive dining experience.\n\nOverall, it's a great place for an authentic omakase experience without the usual hefty price tag. You leave not just with a full stomach, but with a sense of having experienced something special and true to the heart of sushi-making. Definitely worth a visit for anyone who loves sushi and is looking for a unique, low-key dining experience.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten January 29, 2024\nSushi Taka\ncám ơn quý khách đã luôn ủng hộ quán sushi taka, rất hi vọng sẽ được phục vụ quý khách lần sau\n\nkind regards\nSushi Taka Restaurant management\nRead more\nWritten March 24, 2025\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
